# Milestone: M3
# Covers: destroying a Realm cancels all watchers registered in that Realm;
#         pending watcher callbacks do not fire after destruction.
#
# defer-to: M5
#
# Reason: watcher subsystem lands at M5 (reactive-runtime). At M3, Realm
# destroy hook is in place (URealm record created at T14) but there are no
# watchers to cancel yet. Realm-side cancel-on-destroy semantics are already
# verified by tests/unit/test_realm.c (T14).
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by setting up a Realm with an every()
# watcher, destroying the Realm, and verifying the watcher does not fire.
#
# Urbyscript source (activate at M5):
#   [Would require host-driver to instantiate Realm, see realm_isolation.chk.]
#   var called = 0;
#   every(100ms) { called = called + 1 };
#   [Destroy realm here]
#   [Advance time; verify called == 0]
